+### Specialty directory
+
+<a id="req-vet-003"></a>
+
+Beside the veterinarian directory the clinic publishes the specialties it knows (confirmed 2026-08-04). Every specialty the clinic stores is listed under the name stored for it. Under each specialty stand the veterinarians holding it, each named in full — first name then last name, as in "Helen Leary" `[REQ-VET-003]`. The page enumerates specialties, not the veterinarian roster: a veterinarian holding no specialty is named nowhere on it, and a specialty no veterinarian holds is still listed. Every specialty is shown together on one page rather than a page at a time. The view is read-only, and NG-2 stands — neither a specialty nor a veterinarian can be created, changed, or removed from it.
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given the clinic's stored specialties, when the specialty directory is opened, then every one of them is listed under its stored name.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty held by one or more veterinarians, when the directory is opened, then each holder is named beneath it as first name then last name.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty no veterinarian holds, when the directory is opened, then the specialty is still listed, with no veterinarian named beneath it.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian is named nowhere on the page.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given every stored specialty, when the directory is opened, then all of them appear on the one page, with no paging offered.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given the directory, when it is opened, then it offers no action to create, change, or remove a specialty or a veterinarian.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. A veterinarian holding more than one specialty is named beneath each specialty they hold.
+2. The specialties are listed in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one, and so are the veterinarians beneath each specialty.
+3. A specialty name is stored data rather than wording: it renders as stored, whichever language the reader has chosen. The page's own labels are wording and follow REQ-LANG-002.
+
+**Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
